// The same for an absolute path that is not there: a structured IOError
// (SZ4005) and a non-zero exit, not an empty string and not a crash.
//
// As above, this proves nothing about confinement. An absolute path to a file
// that DOES exist is read successfully, wherever it is. This program used to
// name /etc/shadow and claim absolute access "must be rejected"; it passed on
// Windows because the path is absent and would have passed on Linux because the
// file is unreadable by a normal user — in neither case for the stated reason.
//
// See tests/filesystem_reach.rs for what actually happens.
let content = File.read("/__no_such_absolute_file_for_the_path_tests__");
out "FAIL: reading a path that is not there should have failed";
